    "author": "GHL Prime Team",
    "excerpt": "GoHighLevel vs HighLevel confuses almost everyone. Here is the plain-English explainer of why one platform has three names, and where LeadConnector shows up.",
    "cover_image": "",
    "reading_time": 7,
    "content": "<p>If you have spent any time around this platform, you have probably been confused at least once. You signed up for &lsquo;GoHighLevel&rsquo;, but the company calls itself &lsquo;HighLevel&rsquo;, your text messages show up as &lsquo;LeadConnector&rsquo;, and you cannot find your account anywhere in Zapier under the name you expected. So what is going on, and which one is the real one?</p><p>The short answer: GoHighLevel, HighLevel, and LeadConnector are all the <strong>same platform</strong>. They are three names for one product, used in different places for deliberate reasons. Once you understand the logic behind the naming, every confusing label suddenly makes sense. Let&rsquo;s clear it up properly.</p><h2>GoHighLevel vs HighLevel: which name is correct?</h2><p>Both are correct &mdash; they just come from different places.</p><ul><li><strong>HighLevel</strong> is the official company and product name. The business operates at highlevel.com, and that is the brand you will see on invoices, in legal terms, and in official announcements.</li><li><strong>GoHighLevel (or GHL)</strong> is the original domain name and the name the entire community uses. The platform first launched on gohighlevel.com, and that name stuck. Today almost everyone &mdash; agencies, consultants, YouTubers, Facebook groups &mdash; says &lsquo;GoHighLevel&rsquo; or just &lsquo;GHL&rsquo;.</li></ul><p>So when you ask &lsquo;is GoHighLevel the same as HighLevel?&rsquo;, the answer is yes, completely. There is no difference in features, pricing, or accounts. It is the same login, the same dashboard, the same tool. HighLevel is simply the tidier official brand; GoHighLevel is the name that history and habit gave it. You can use either and nobody will misunderstand you.</p><h2>So why is GoHighLevel called LeadConnector?</h2><p>This is where most people get tripped up, and it is the most interesting part of the story. <strong>LeadConnector</strong> is a third name, but it is not a different company or a different product. It is HighLevel&rsquo;s neutral, white-label brand &mdash; the identity the platform wears when it needs to stay invisible.</p><p>Here is the reason it exists. HighLevel was built as a white-label-first platform. Its core customers are agencies who resell the software to their own clients under their own brand. An agency might sell &lsquo;Acme Marketing CRM&rsquo; to a local dentist, and that dentist should never see the words &lsquo;HighLevel&rsquo; or &lsquo;GoHighLevel&rsquo; anywhere. If they did, the agency&rsquo;s branding would fall apart and the client could simply go buy the platform directly.</p><p>To make that possible, HighLevel uses the neutral name <strong>LeadConnector</strong> for all the public-facing infrastructure that an agency cannot fully customise. It is a deliberately generic name that gives nothing away.</p><h2>Where you actually encounter LeadConnector</h2><p>LeadConnector is not something you choose or sign up for separately. It appears automatically in specific places. Here is where you will run into it.</p><ul><li><strong>The mobile app.</strong> The default app in the App Store and Google Play is called &lsquo;LeadConnector&rsquo;. It is the same app as the HighLevel mobile app, just neutrally branded so agency clients can download it without seeing the parent name. (Agencies can pay extra for a fully custom-branded app under their own name.)</li><li><strong>Email and SMS sending.</strong> The built-in communication services are branded &lsquo;LC Email&rsquo; and &lsquo;LC Phone&rsquo; &mdash; LC standing for LeadConnector. These are HighLevel&rsquo;s own sending infrastructure, replacing third-party tools like Mailgun and Twilio.</li><li><strong>Caller ID and texting.</strong> When a message or call goes out and the number has not been verified to a custom name, recipients may see &lsquo;LeadConnector&rsquo; on caller ID or in message records. That is simply the platform&rsquo;s neutral identity showing through.</li><li><strong>Integration listings.</strong> In Zapier, Make, and similar tools, the app is listed as &lsquo;LeadConnector&rsquo; &mdash; not &lsquo;GoHighLevel&rsquo;. This is the single most common reason people think their integration is missing.</li></ul><h2>Common confusions, answered plainly</h2><h3>Why does my texting show LeadConnector?</h3><p>Because LC Phone is the sending service powering your texts, and &lsquo;LeadConnector&rsquo; is its neutral brand. It is not a different company intercepting your messages &mdash; it is HighLevel&rsquo;s own infrastructure. With proper number registration and branded sender setup, you can reduce or remove that label so your business name shows instead.</p><h3>Why can&rsquo;t I find GoHighLevel in Zapier?</h3><p>Because it is not listed under that name. Search Zapier for <strong>&lsquo;LeadConnector&rsquo;</strong> instead, and you will find it immediately. Same platform, neutral listing name. This trips up almost everyone the first time they try to connect an automation.</p><h3>Is LeadConnector a scam or is it legit?</h3><p>It is completely legit. LeadConnector <em>is</em> HighLevel &mdash; the same company, the same platform, just wearing its white-label name. If you see charges, apps, or messages branded &lsquo;LeadConnector&rsquo; and you use GoHighLevel, that is expected and normal, not a sign of fraud.</p><h2>A quick FAQ</h2><h3>Is GoHighLevel the same as HighLevel?</h3><p>Yes. Identical platform. HighLevel is the official name; GoHighLevel is the original domain and community name.</p><h3>Do I need to choose between HighLevel, GoHighLevel, and LeadConnector?</h3><p>No. You sign up for one platform and get all three identities depending on context. There is nothing to pick.</p><h3>Will my clients see &lsquo;HighLevel&rsquo; anywhere?</h3><p>If you set up white-label branding correctly, no. That is the entire point of the LeadConnector layer &mdash; it keeps the parent name hidden so your brand stays front and centre.</p><h2>The takeaway</h2><p>One platform, three names: <strong>HighLevel</strong> (official), <strong>GoHighLevel / GHL</strong> (community and original domain), and <strong>LeadConnector</strong> (the neutral white-label brand for apps, sending, and integrations). The naming feels messy until you see the logic &mdash; it is built so agencies can resell the software invisibly. Once you know that, every confusing label becomes a feature, not a bug.</p><p>Getting these pieces configured correctly &mdash; LC Phone and Email set up, sender branding clean, and white-label branding airtight so your clients never see the wrong name &mdash; is exactly where a proper build pays off. If you want it done right the first time, take a look at our <a href='/services/ghl-setup'>GHL setup service</a>, or <a href='/contact'>get in touch</a> and we will help you map it out.</p>",
